  "status": "candidate record. The menu reads Home, Build your AI brain, Build your AI GTM, Success stories, Ideas you can use, Quick AI tips, Questions we get asked, About us and Media in every menu and footer; the four renamed pages carry their label as their title; /about is a new indexed page.",
  "scopeRequested": "Krish, 2026-09-25, with a screenshot of the open menu and a headshot: \"In the menu, Rename Results to Success Stories, Thinking to Ideas You Can Use, Questions leaders ask to Quick AI tips, Before you start to Questions we get asked, and add Home at the top. Change the titles inside the pages too. And then add a new page called About us, which will contain my profile (build this from krishraja.com and with this headshot, substantiate why I'm bulding this business and make me sound incredibly warm and approachable. Follow the existing design system\". The plan (sentence-case labels matching the existing door labels; About us before Media; page H1, document title and pages.mjs headline set to the label; the headshot under src/assets/founder; career facts from krishraja.com only; no count of leaders helped) was approved before implementation.",
  "sessionDecisions": [
    "PRIMARY_ROUTES in src/lib/publicLinks.ts is the one list: Home (/), Build your AI brain, Build your AI GTM, Success stories (/case-studies), Ideas you can use (/blog), Quick AI tips (/answers), Questions we get asked (/faq), About us (/about), Media (the subscription, badged). The shell menu and footer map it; the generated homepage menus and footer carry the same list through authorised corrections in scripts/qa/build-homepage-release.mjs, with drift counts for Home, About us, the four renamed labels and zero retired labels. The R3 prototype tree is untouched. primary-routes-parity.test.ts holds the two menus together and pins Home first and About us second to last.",
    "Each renamed page carries its label as its H1, its document title and its pages.mjs title and headline, so the click lands where it said: /case-studies \"Success stories.\" (was \"Proof you can inspect.\" on the page and \"The decision, and what changed next.\" in the head), /blog \"Ideas you can use\" (its H1 already said so), /answers \"Quick AI tips.\", /faq \"Questions we get asked.\". Descriptions are unchanged. Social plates repainted only for the three changed headlines and the new page.",
    "/about: src/pages/About.tsx in the shell, indexed, prerendered and in the sitemap and llms.txt. It opens in the practice's we, then Krish speaks in the first person beside the supplied headshot (src/assets/founder/krish-about.webp, 1022x1222, kept out of public/), using the founder block's plate, name line and measure from mindmake-instruments.css and a small page sheet, src/styles/mindmake-about.css. Facts are his own published record at krishraja.com: sixteen years across Microsoft, Nine, SingTel and Captify; Nine $9M to $61M, Captify Australia zero to $12M a year, SingTel $4M to $38M across twelve markets; fourteen agents; his degrees and Harvard Business School Executive Education. They are career history, never client results. Three career references (Lizzie Young, Ashley Wales-Brown, Matt Paine) are read from src/data/testimonials.ts by id, verbatim, as 04_PROOF.md permits on the about surface. No count of leaders helped. The page is the fourth named surface in the Krish gate; its description carries no name because llms.txt and the head are not named surfaces.",
    "The handoff manifest's sharedLanguage selection and its check carry the new labels with a provenance note; the earlier labels are preserved in that note and in history/LOG.md. STATE.md non-regression item 8 lists the new labels."
